# DTF tier manifest: proxy-egress
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + squid (the outbound egress proxy topology).
# The ONLY topology on which issue #2570 (fail-closed SSRF DNS guard blocking the
# CONFIGURED egress proxy's own private IP) can manifest: the backend is forced
# to make every outbound fetch through a proxy whose address is private.
# Oracle: the two-half discriminating gate (legit egress-through-proxy WORKS;
# a genuine SSRF upstream is still REFUSED).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives several admin create/delete +
# test-upstream calls back-to-back through a single admin; the base default (ON)
# would throttle them. (The base default stays ON; a tier that must disable a
# shipped control does so explicitly, per design section 2.2 — same as the
# isolation tier.)
PROFILES="storage.filesystem proxy.squid"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
